# Git writes LF on checkout whatever the clone's core.autocrlf says. A clone that
# writes CRLF reads every file as changed, and stages a whole-file rewrite of the
# repository in place of the work.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Below the line above, because a later line overrides an earlier one. The hook is
# run by sh. Checked out with CRLF it fails as a bad interpreter.
hooks/** text eol=lf
